---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
---

<Prose
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles data, cookies and advertising.`}
  lede="The short version: we don't ask you for anything, we don't run our own tracking, and the only third party that sets cookies here is our advertising provider."
  updated="8 August 2026"
>
  <p>
    This policy explains what happens to data when you visit
    <strong>{SITE.domain}</strong> ("the site", "we", "us"). It applies to every
    page on this domain.
  </p>

  <h2>1. What we collect ourselves</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing that identifies you. The site is a set of static pages. There is no
    account system, no login, no comment box and no newsletter sign-up, so there
    is no personal information for us to store.
  </p>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider keeps standard server logs (IP address, browser type,
    the page requested, the time of the request) for a short period for
    security and abuse prevention. We do not use those logs to build a profile
    of you and we do not sell them.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
  <p>
    We do not set our own cookies for analytics or personalisation. Cookies on
    this site come from third parties, described below. Your browser lets you
    block or delete cookies at any time — that will not break the site.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Advertising</h2>
  <p>
    This site is funded by advertising and uses <strong>Google AdSense</strong>,
    a third-party advertising service provided by Google LLC.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on
      your prior visits to this site or other sites.
    </li>
    <li>
      Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve
      ads to you based on your visit to this and/or other sites on the internet.
    </li>
    <li>
      You may opt out of personalised advertising by visiting
      <a href="https://www.google.com/settings/ads" rel="nofollow noopener"
        >Google Ads Settings</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      You can also opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for
      personalised advertising at
      <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" rel="nofollow noopener"
        >aboutads.info/choices</a
      > or, in Europe, at
      <a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" rel="nofollow noopener"
        >youronlinechoices.eu</a
      >.
    </li>
    <li>
      Where required, third-party vendors we work with may collect and use data
      under a consent framework. If you are in a region that requires consent
      (such as the EEA or the UK), you will be shown a consent message before
      personalised ads are served, and you can change your choice at any time.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Google's own explanation of how it uses data from sites that use its
    services is at
    <a
      href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites"
      rel="nofollow noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a
    >.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Fonts</h2>
  <p>
    We load one display typeface from Google Fonts. When your browser requests
    it, Google receives your IP address as part of that request. No cookie is
    set by the font request itself.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Guides sometimes link to manufacturers, standards bodies or retailers. Once
    you follow a link you are on someone else's site under their privacy policy,
    not ours. We are not responsible for their practices.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Children</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly
    collect information from them. If you believe a child has provided us with
    personal information, contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct,
    delete or restrict the use of personal data held about you, and to object to
    processing or withdraw consent. Because we do not hold identifiable data
    ourselves, most of these requests are best directed to Google, whose ad
    services set the cookies described above. If you'd like help, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> with "Privacy" in the
    subject line.
  </p>
  <p>
    California residents: we do not sell or share personal information as those
    terms are defined by the CCPA/CPRA.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes we will update the date at the top of this page.
    Material changes will be noted on the page for at least 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a
    >.
  </p>
</Prose>
